   258	
   259	## Row 3's product-facing contract (council rounds 120 to 122; A1, clamping, withdrawn)
   260	
   261	**The rule.**
   262	
   263	- **On every store with a `days_completed` table**, finished or not, partial rows or not, an explicit upper bound later than the last
   264	  completed day is refused. The same date gets the same answer whenever it is asked.
   265	- An omitted bound gives the last completed day, as today.
   266	- **Steps but no completed day:** refused as the first day.
   267	- **`days_completed` present with no steps and no completed day** (an empty new store): read as today. An omitted bound gives what
   268	  `default_as_of` gives today (none), and an explicit bound passes.
   269	- **A legacy ledger without the tables:** read as today.
   270	- **Ranges:**
   271	  - `changes(since, to)` excludes its start, so a `since` on or after the resolved `to` is refused;
   272	  - `history(from, to)` includes its start, so a `from` after the resolved `to` is refused and `from` equal to `to` passes.
   273	
   274	**The owner, and what the structural check enforces.**
   275	
   276	- `service.resolve_bound(conn, bound)` raises `FirstDayNotCompleted` or `BoundNotCompleted(requested, last_completed_day)` and is
   277	  idempotent: a bound it has already passed passes again.
   278	- **Every public function that takes a date resolves it at its entry through `resolve_bound`:**
   279	  - `service`: `summaries`, `views`, `view`, `evidence`, `history`, `record`, `changes`, `evaluate`;
   280	  - `bundle`: `not_judged`, `view_bundle`, `days`, `thesis_bundles`, `library`;
   281	  - `idea.read_idea` and `search.search`.
   282	- Nested calls pass a resolved bound, which resolves again unchanged. That covers `view_bundle` called directly with no date (as
   283	  `scripts/mock_data.py` does), or from `_bundles` and `idea.read_idea`.
   284	- **Internal helpers that take a date** (`dependencies`, `dependants`, `evidence_record`, `is_open_as_of`, `state_as_of`, `visible`,
   285	  `_bundles`, …) receive a resolved bound and refuse `None`.
   286	- **The structural check** reads every function of `service`, `bundle`, `search` and `idea` with a date parameter (`as_of`,
   287	  `to_day`). Each must either call `resolve_bound` or be named in the check's list of internal helpers, which refuse `None`.
   288	  - A function in neither, or a bound resolved by `or default_as_of(...)`, fails the suite.
   289	  - The check's own mutant (a new public function without the call) must fail it.
   290	
   291	**The response, per channel.**
   292	
   293	| Channel | First day not completed | Bound after the last completed day | Range start not before its end |
   294	|---|---|---|---|
   295	| API | 503 `{"error": "the store's first day has not completed"}` | 409 `{"error": "day not completed", "requested": X, "last_completed_day": Y}` | 409 `{"error": "range start not before its end", "start": S, "end": T}` |
   296	| MCP tools | a tool error whose message carries the same fields | the same | the same |
   297	| Streamed Idea route | the status and body, before any header | the same | — |
   298	
   299	- `error_response` returns `(status, payload)`. The two new exceptions get the payloads above, and every other error keeps
   300	  `{"error": message}`. `_answer` and `_stream_answer` send the payload as given.
   301	- **The streamed route, in one transaction:**
   302	  - it opens its connections, begins the read transaction and resolves the bound and first-day check;
   303	  - **only then** does it send its 200 headers and run the Idea work in the same transaction, which it ends after;
   304	  - a refusal is sent as a normal status and body before any header.
   305	  - The Idea work includes model calls, so this transaction lasts the whole request, up to minutes. That is within row 5's
   306	    one-request rule, and it holds back a checkpoint that long.
   307	
   308	**Callers.**
   309	
   310	- **The page, when its live library read succeeds:** it sends only days from the served dataset (`library.getDay()` to `/ideas`;
   311	  the returned `card.idea.as_of` to `/thesis-bundles`). These are never after the last completed day.
   312	- **The page, when its live library read fails:**
   313	  - it keeps its embedded snapshot silently (as `thesis-ui.md` specifies), and that snapshot's day can be later than the service's
   314	    last completed day;
   315	  - `/ideas` is then refused with 409, and the page shows its existing Idea error naming no day;
   316	  - this is documented here and tested; it is not claimed impossible.
   317	- **MCP clients and direct API users with a later date:**
   318	  - on the running product's store, they would get an error naming 2026-08-28 instead of today's half-processed 2026-08-29 (99
   319	    evidence records, 117 links);
   320	  - on a finished store, they would get an error instead of today's identical answer.
   321	  - This is the behaviour change, recorded for Alex.
   322	- **Not deployed:** no running service is restarted. D439 does not authorize a deploy, and the change reaches the running product
   323	  only on a restart, which is on Alex's page.
   324	
   325	**Proofs added to the plan (2b to 2e):**
   326	
   327	- 2b. The structural check, and its mutant.
   328	- 2c. Each public function called directly with a future bound, an omitted one and a past one, on the four store states: finished,
   329	  partial, first day, and empty with tables. A copy of the served store's state is included.
   330	- 2d. The ranges: `changes` with `since` equal to its end is refused; `history` with `from` equal to `to` passes.
   331	- 2e. The streamed route on a first-day store and with a future date: a status before any header. With a writer committing during
   332	  an Idea request, the request's data are the state at its start.
   333	- 2f. The page verifier (`poc/ui/verify-*.mjs`): live read successful, then the Idea call succeeds; live read failed with a later
   334	  embedded day, then the Idea error shows and nothing else breaks.
   335	
   336	## Not covered
   337	
   338	- Resuming a stopped live store.
   339	- The Idea planner on a new-system ledger.
   340	- A long-running service's restart and monitoring.
   341	- The page's note when its live read fails, which is Alex's presentation choice.
